-- title:
--   Kernel degree p² for Pi under isogeny from a special module
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a field equipped with a ring homomorphism $j_0$ from $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ (written `Zp2 p`) to $k$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$, i.e. a commutative two-dimensional formal group law together with series endomorphisms $\mathrm{act}(a)$ for $a \in \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = \mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a) = \mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ for the Witt-vector Frobenius $\sigma$. Assume $\Phi$ is special with respect to $j_0$, that is, the two submodules $\Phi.\mathrm{lieZero}\,j_0$ and $\Phi.\mathrm{lieOne}\,j_0$ are complementary and each invertible as $k$-modules, and that $\Phi$ has height $4$: the algebra $\mathrm{KerAlgebra}$ of $\mathrm{act}(p)$ (the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by the ideal generated by the components of the series) is finite and projective over $k$ and has fibre dimension $p^4$ over every field receiving $k$. Let $L$ be a Noetherian commutative ring in which $p$ is nilpotent, $f : k \to L/pL$ a ring homomorphism, $X$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $L$, $\rho$ a pair of power series over $L/pL$ and $h$ a natural number such that $\rho$ is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from the base change $\Phi\otimes_{k,f} L/pL$ to the reduction of $X$ modulo $pL$ whose kernel algebra is finite, projective and of fibre dimension $p^h$. Then $\varpi_X$ has kernel of degree $p^2$: the kernel algebra of $X.\mathrm{varpi}$ is a finite projective $L$-module whose base change to any field $\kappa$ along any ring homomorphism $L \to \kappa$ has $\kappa$-dimension $p^2$.
--
--   This is the statement, in Drinfeld's theory of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, that the uniformiser endomorphism $\Pi$ of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module whose reduction modulo $p$ receives an isogeny from a special height-$4$ module over a field has finite locally free kernel of order $p^2$. It is used in the rigidification step for fake elliptic curves, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia).
